@4.5 BMX.INC.BL -- a BMX bitmap into VERA
.
=4.5 BMX.INC.BL -- A BMX BITMAP INTO VERA
.
=DESCRIPTION
.
.  BMX.OPEN
.      IN: BMX.FILE$
.      OUT: BMX.ERROR$, and the header -- BMX.WIDTH .HEIGHT .DEPTH .VERSION
.        .PALUSED .PALFIRST .DATAOFF .PACKED
.
.  BMX.PAINT
.      IN: an open file
.      OUT: palette and pixels in VRAM, file closed
.
.  BMX.SHOW
.      IN: BMX.FILE$
.      OUT: both of the above
.
.  BMX.CLOSE
.      IN: --
.      OUT: abandons a file opened by BMX.OPEN
.
.  BMX.RESTORE
.      IN: --
.      OUT: puts the machine's own palette back
.
.BMX.ERROR$ empty means it worked.
.
:BMX.FILE$ = "TITLE.BMX"
:SCREEN 128
:GOSUB BMX.SHOW
:IF BMX.ERROR$ <> "" THEN PRINT BMX.ERROR$
.
.Use the long form to read the size before committing to a screen mode, or to
.report a bad file before the display is torn down:
.
:BMX.FILE$ = F$
:GOSUB BMX.OPEN
:IF BMX.ERROR$ <> "" THEN GOTO COMPLAIN
:' ... BMX.WIDTH, BMX.HEIGHT, BMX.PALUSED readable here ...
:SCREEN 128
:GOSUB BMX.PAINT
.
.Set the screen mode before BMX.PAINT, not after. SCREEN reloads the default
.palette, so a mode change after painting discards the image's colours:
.correct pixels, wrong palette.
.
.BMX.PAINT writes the image's colours over the machine's palette, and nothing
.on the X16 restores them -- not SCREEN, not the KERNAL's screen_mode.
.BMX.PAINT therefore stashes all 256 entries in spare VRAM first, and
.BMX.RESTORE writes them back:
.
:BMX.FILE$ = "TITLE.BMX"
:SCREEN 128
:GOSUB BMX.SHOW
:' ... the title screen ...
:GOSUB BMX.RESTORE
.
.A program that keeps the machine need never call it. A program that returns
.the machine to BASIC or chains to another calls it once. It is safe to call
.at any time: with nothing stashed there is nothing to do, so a program whose
.image failed to load can still call it on the way out. All 256 entries are
.kept, not the range the file claims, and they are kept once per run -- so a
.slideshow restores the machine's own palette rather than the previous
.image's.
.
.BMX.STASH is the VRAM address they go to, $13000 by default, which is free
.above the 320x240 framebuffer in the mode this module paints into. A caller
.using tiles, sprites or a second bitmap there must move it or switch it off
.with BMX.STASH = -1. The address is checked: a stash inside the bitmap or
.overlapping the PSG registers is reported and nothing is painted.
.
.Use -1 to switch it off, not 0. Zero is what the variable holds before it is
.set, and BMX.INIT runs at the first BMX.OPEN, after a caller would have set
.it, so 0 has to keep meaning unset.
.
.The module handles 8 bits per pixel, uncompressed, which is what SCREEN 128
.displays without a decompressor. Anything else is reported rather than
.attempted. The image is centred, and anything larger than 320x240 is
.clipped.
.
.Examples: BMXVIEW.EXP.BL, and BMXPAL.EXP.BL for the palette
.
=EXAMPLE PROGRAM
.
.  BMXVIEW.EXP.BL -- runnable, in the GPC-BASIC folder
.  BMXPAL.EXP.BL -- runnable, in the GPC-BASIC folder
.
=SEE ALSO
.
>44|4.5 BMX.INC.BL -- a BMX bitmap into VERA
